  "report_period": "Week 45 (30th Oct to 6th Nov 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Pan Ocean have committed their Capesize \"Pan Advance\" 179/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 06/2029, DD 07/2027, Scrubber fitted) to UAE interests at USD 35,3 mill. Remind you that the \"Navios Pollux\" 180/2009 Stx, Korea (SS 07/2029, DD 11/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 30,75 mill. In addition, the one-year-older \"Ladycharm\" 169/2008 Daehan, Korea (SS 09/2028, DD 12/2026) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 27 mill. The Post Panamax \"Carl Oldendorff\" 93/2011 Taizhou, China (SS 05/2030, DD 04/2027, Scrubber fitted) of Oldendorff Carriers was committed at USD 16,5 mill. Note that a month ago, the \"LC Milady\" 93/2011 Shanhaiguan, China (SS/DD 09/2026) was sold at USD 14,5 mill. Japanese owners committed the Ultramax \"Diamond Queen\" 61/2013 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS 05/2031, DD 03/2029) to undisclosed interests at USD 24,8 mill. For reference, the two-years-older sister vessel \"Amis Wisdom VI\" 61/2011 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) was sold in July at USD 22 mill. On the Supramax sector, following the acquisition of the \"Kristinita\" 58/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 07/2031, DD 05/2029) in October at xs USD 20 mill, clients of ADNOC L&S have now acquired the sister vessel \"SW Mistral I\" 58/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 05/2031, DD 05/2029) at USD 20 mill. The Handysize \"Fuga\" 38/2012 Shimanami, Japan (SS 09/2030, DD 11/2028) was committed to Vietnamese interests at low USD 19 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Locomotion\" 38/2013 Shimanami, Japan (SS 12/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold in October at USD 19,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Dynacom Tankers have committed their Suezmax \"Fleves\" 158/2012 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to client of BGN at USD 110 mill. Note that a month ago, the \"Almi Galaxy\" 157/2012 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) was sold at USD 92 mill. The LR2 \"Haima\" 105/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 03/2029, DD 04/2027) of Mitsui OSK Lines was committed to Greek interests at USD 65 mill. For reference, the Korean Aframax \"Eurointegrity\" 105/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 02/2029, DD 03/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 60 mill. Vietnamese owners committed the MR2 \"LS Neptune\" 50/2007 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 20,2 mill. By way of comparison, the sister vessel \"Valle Azzurra\" 50/2007 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 12/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 20 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route moved slightly lower, with Dampier and Port Hedland fixtures settling between USD 13.25/13.80 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, held firm levels between USD 35.50/37.00 fio. A long- haul departure from Seven Islands to Qingdao reached USD 41.50 fio, while Saldanha Bay to Qingdao achieved USD 27.10 fio. In the transatlantic market, a Ponta Da Madeira run to Rotterdam fixed at USD 17.25 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan and Japan options settled between USD 19,250/24,000 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, South East Asia and Singapore-Japan ranges fetched between USD 17,500/25,000 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China, India and Singapore- Japan ranges achieved between USD 14,000/21,800 pd. In the Atlantic, long- haul departures from Continent via USEC to India and Japan/South Korea ranges obtained strong levels between USD 25,000/26,250 pd. On period, a Kamsarmax delivering in North China fixed for 4 to 6 months duration worldwide at USD 19,100 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, regional departures from South China and North China to ECI and North China range settled between USD 20,500/29,000 pd, while a regional clinker run within SE Asia fetched USD 32,000 pd. Out of USWC, a NoPac trip to Far East reached USD 30,000 pd and a long-haul departure from North China to West Africa made USD 26,000 pd. An East Australia petcoke run to East Med obtained USD 28,000 pd. From West Coast India, regional salt and clinker trips to ECI and China ranges fixed between USD 14,000/19,000 pd, while a South Africa coal run to ECI achieved USD 22,000 pd alongside a USD 220,000 ballast bonus. In the Continent, scrap to East Med and wheat to West Africa settled between USD 24,000/33,000 pd. In the Atlantic, US Gulf front-haul petcoke and grain trips to India and China ranges ranged between USD 27,000/34,500 pd, while transatlantic grain and wood pellet runs from USEC and US Gulf to Med and Continent ranges fixed between USD 24,000/28,750 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Atlantic, US Gulf and USEC grain, pellet and coal departures to Continent, Mediterranean and regional destinations fixed between USD 16,750/21,000 pd. Continent grain runs to West Africa achieved USD 26,000 pd, while a Black Sea urea trip to Continent made USD 12,250 pd. Out of West Africa, fertilizer and grain runs via ECSA to Brazil and West Med range settled between USD 14,000/15,000 pd. From NCSA, a transatlantic departure to Continent range reached USD 25,250 pd."
    }
  },
